//Abstraction
Abstraction means hiding unnecessary implementation details and showing only the essential functionality.

Example:

class Car {
public:
    void start() {
        cout << "Car started";
    }

private:
    void checkEngine() {
        cout << "Checking engine";
    }
};

When we do:

Car c;
c.start();

We only need to know what start() does.

We don't need to know the internal details of checkEngine() or how the car actually starts.

Simple real-life example

When you use an ATM:

You enter PIN
Select withdrawal
Get money

You don't need to know the internal banking process.

That's abstraction.

Simple definition

Abstraction = hiding implementation details and exposing only the necessary functionality.